From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: j7prime p3 <p3@j7prime.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: exynos7870: let CMU_ISP power down

Nothing uses the ISP (camera) block, but most of its clocks are marked
critical. Once CMU_ISP sits in the ISP power domain, a critical clock
keeps the CMU runtime-active and the domain powered for good.

Drop the critical flags so the domain can stay off until a camera
driver needs it. The domain only completes its power-down while its
input clocks from CMU_MIF run (with them gated its status stops half
way, 0xc); the vendor kernel ungates them before each power-down. Keep
them running instead.

j7prime: on the J7 Prime the ISP PLL runs at 533 MHz with its gates
enabled and no consumer (clk_summary, 7.3.4-j7p1).

Origin: Martin Štrobl, github.com/a3y17lte-mainline/kernel_samsung_exynos7870 (branch lineage-24.0) commit 32142e0f36e9.
---

Notes:
    Port to v7.3.4 + j7prime 0001-0017: applied with offsets.

 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos7870.c | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++------------------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

